index 0000000..449ef96
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/engineering/H1_PRIVATE_PACS_READS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# Canonical H1 image custody with optional private PACS reads
+
+Status: synthetic engineering candidate, not production or clinical clearance.
+Base: PR #242 at `0c57f9fe86ef3ef12d24e1fd2a883dd80ddd7a3d` (image custody),
+on #222. No new schema, migration, image ID, route, action or dependency.
+
+## Ownership
+
+`PostgresSourceImages` remains the authority for original objects and their
+explicit source-version links. The optional operator-injected `image_archive`
+port retrieves only server-stored Study/Series/SOP identifiers. End users do
+not select URLs, archive credentials or hashes. An enabled remote archive
+must return the exact immutable canonical original; failures never silently
+fall back to PostgreSQL. The normal local-custody mode remains unchanged.
+
+Preflight locks the existing patient/case/source owner, validates original
+custody and refreshes authorization. Network I/O occurs outside the transaction.
+A fresh transaction then revalidates the same patient/source/binding revision,
+compares remote and canonical bytes, and commits the existing authorized-read
+receipt before returning an attachment. A source amendment, lost grant, changed
+actor, corrupted bytes or failed audit write withholds the result. Receipts
+prove prepared disclosure, not delivery or atomic external revocation.
+
+## Isolated actual backend test
+
+`tools/imaging/verify_h1_private_pacs.py` uses the unmodified pinned research
+PACSNode commit `e9b4334477a66967d290add9e0b9afa068f59dc0`. It runs in a disposable
+Linux network namespace with only loopback, drops root before starting PACS,
+and exposes no host TCP HTTP or DIMSE listener. A private 0700 directory/0600
+Unix socket carries only fixed original-instance requests with a service-only
+OIDC token. Patient credentials never reach PACS. The test checks actual kernel
+PACS namespace identity and inability to connect to both raw ports from the
+API/client host. This is not whole-host isolation against root or same-UID
+compromise, nor a production gateway installation.
+
+The same independently authored synthetic objects are uploaded to PACS and
+imported through #242's existing HTTP custody endpoint. Real H1/PG16 retrieval
+then verifies original bytes, cross-patient/case/purpose and missing-grant denial,
+late revocation/amendment, API/database restart and PostgreSQL dump/restore.
+Existing source/image tests remain; no alternate image database is introduced.
+
+## Reconciliation and limits
+
+A parallel custody candidate was stopped after discovering the completed #242
+owner. Its new migration and image routes are not included here. #234's newer
+source-projection integrity and #238's separate migration branch still need
+owner-reviewed convergence; this change does not silently claim that merge.
+
+PACSNode remains HOLD: source/asset/crate rights, DICOMweb conformance, broad
+image profiles, compressed decoding, production accounts/consent, clinical
+validation and general viewer/rendered/bulk-data workflows are not approved.
+The code-only pydicom runtime and its existing 25-wheel gate are unchanged.
+Only the existing bounded uncompressed CT profile is supported. No real patient
+data, model inference, diagnostic decisions, merge or deployment is authorized.
